distribution. It is not covered by the LICENSE file and no rights to it are
granted here. Enquiries: https://seclume.space/

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party code
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

seclume implements the PostgreSQL, MySQL, TDS and Oracle TTC wire protocols
itself and depends on nothing outside the JDK at runtime. The Spring Boot
starter depends on Spring, which the application brings anyway.

Oracle native network encryption (seclume-oracle, the advanced negotiation and
the encryption and checksums of each packet) follows the implementation in
go-ora (https://github.com/sijms/go-ora), Copyright (c) 2020 Samy Sultan,
licensed under the MIT License. The licence text is in
licenses/go-ora-MIT.txt.

Parts of the Oracle driver (seclume-oracle) are derived from python-oracledb
(https://github.com/oracle/python-oracledb), version 4.0.2,
Copyright (c) 2016, 2026 Oracle and/or its affiliates, dual-licensed under the
Universal Permissive License (UPL) 1.0 and the Apache License, Version 2.0:
the password verifiers and session key derivation of the login, the layout of
OSON (binary JSON) and VECTOR values, and details of the TTC messages. Which
parts, and how, is recorded in PROVENANCE.md and at the places in the source
that use them. The licence text, as python-oracledb publishes it, is in
licenses/python-oracledb-LICENSE.txt; python-oracledb's own NOTICE reads:
"Copyright (c) 2016, 2026, Oracle and/or its affiliates."

Data, not code: seclume-core carries Amazon RDS's public CA certificate bundle
(space/seclume/internal/aws-rds-global-bundle.pem), as published by Amazon Web
Services at https://truststore.pki.rds.amazonaws.com/global/global-bundle.pem,
so that tlsRootCert=aws-rds can verify RDS servers. The certificates are public
trust anchors and are redistributed unchanged.

Data, not code: seclume-core carries the Public Suffix List
(https://publicsuffix.org/), maintained by the Mozilla Foundation and its
contributors and licensed under the Mozilla Public License, Version 2.0, so that
a TLS wildcard never spans a public suffix. Its licence text travels with it
(space/seclume/tls/public-suffix-LICENSE.txt).

Test data: seclume-core/src/test/resources/wycheproof carries test vectors from
Project Wycheproof (https://github.com/C2SP/wycheproof), Copyright Google LLC
and the Wycheproof authors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
They are used by the tests only, redistributed unchanged, and not part of any
published artifact.

Test and build tooling (JUnit, Spring Boot, Flyway, Maven plugins) is declared
in the POMs and carries its own licences; none of it is redistributed here.
JasperReports (LGPL-3.0) is a test dependency of seclume-jasperreports-proof
only, a module that is neither installed nor published.
